After controlling for incident severity, average claim amounts were
similar between fraudulent and non-fraudulent claims within each severity category.

### Key Observation

The higher average cost of fraudulent claims appears to be largely driven by the concentration of fraud
within Major Damage incidents rather than fraud itself increasing claim amounts.


